## Traceability Requirements

### The Traceability Chain

The following chain must be complete and bidirectional at phase completion:

```
System Requirements (input — read-only)
    │
    ▼  (decomposition — documented in HLR files)
High-Level Requirements (HLRs)
    │
    ▼  (refinement — documented in LLR files, DAL C+ only)
Low-Level Requirements (LLRs)
    │
    ▼  (design — documented in DES files)
Software Design
    │
    ▼  (implementation — @req/@design annotations in source)
Source Code
    │
    ▼  (build — controlled by CM, compiler qualified if needed)
Executable Object Code
    │
    ▼  (source-to-object traceability — DAL A only)
Target Executable

    ═══════════════════════════════════════

Requirements (HLR + LLR)
    │
    ▼  (test derivation — documented in TST case files)
Test Cases & Procedures
    │
    ▼  (execution — results in test/results/)
Test Results
    │
    ▼  (coverage analysis — reports in test/coverage/)
Structural Coverage
```

### Traceability Matrix Maintenance

The master traceability matrix (`trace/trace-matrix.md`) is a living artifact. It must be updated whenever:

- A requirement is added, modified, or deleted
- A design element is added, modified, or deleted
- A source code module is added, modified, or deleted
- A test case is added, modified, or deleted
- A derived requirement is identified

**The agent should check and update the traceability matrix as part of every task.** Gaps discovered during work must be reported immediately, not deferred.

### Derived Requirements Register

All derived requirements are tracked in `trace/derived-register.md` with:

| Field | Required |
|-------|----------|
| Derived Req ID | Yes |
| Source (which artifact introduced it) | Yes |
| Rationale | Yes |
| Safety Impact Assessment | Yes |
| Status (OPEN / ASSESSED / ACCEPTED) | Yes |
| System Safety Review Date | When assessed |

