### AI Agent as Tool

The AI agent used on this project is classified as a **DO-330 Criterion 1 tool** (its output becomes part of the deliverable software). Full DO-330 qualification is not pursued due to the non-deterministic nature of LLM-based agents.

**Compensating verification approach**: All AI-generated output is subject to 100% of the verification activities that would apply to human-written artifacts. No verification process is eliminated, reduced, or automated by the agent's involvement. Therefore, DO-330 tool qualification is not required because the tool provides no process credit.

This means:
- AI-generated requirements are independently reviewed by a human
- AI-generated design is independently reviewed by a human
- AI-generated code is independently reviewed by a human and subject to full static analysis, requirements-based testing, and structural coverage analysis
- AI-generated test cases are independently reviewed by a human
- The AI agent never signs off on its own output

